WHY THE RUN FAILED
  After the gallery rebuild the agent began an unrequested browser
  screenshot/critique loop: it hit the missing-browser error from shoot-site.sh,
  followed Playwright's suggestion to run `npx playwright install chromium`,
  installed the browser mid-run, and then spent its remaining turns on a
  render -> read PNG -> tweak -> re-render cycle across index.html and
  demo.html. That loop consumed 35 of the 80 turns and the run hit the cap
  before recording anything. pipeline.md never asked for it; the prompt came
  from the frontend-design skill's "critique your own work, taking screenshots
  if your environment supports it."

  Fixed same-day:
   - pipeline.md Step 8 is now an explicit checkpoint that must finish before
     any optional work, and the visual check is a new hard-capped Step 9
     (2 captures, 3 edits, 1 re-capture, skip if no browser, never install).
   - shoot-site.sh preflights for an installed browser and exits 3 with
     SHOOT_NO_BROWSER rather than surfacing Playwright's "run npx playwright
     install" banner.
   - gen-image.sh retries 3x with backoff on 429/5xx and only charges the daily
     cap for calls that actually returned an image.
